What are the types of authentication in Node js?
===========================================
Node.js supports multiple authentication methods depending on the application requirement.

1️⃣ Username & Password Authentication (Basic)
User logs in using username/email and password
Server verifies credentials from the database
Passwords are stored in hashed format
👉 Commonly used for simple applications
Example:
Email + Password → Verify → Login

2️⃣ Token-Based Authentication (JWT) ⭐ Most Common
After login, server generates a JWT token
Token is sent to the client
Client sends token in every request
Server verifies token
👉 Used in REST APIs, mobile apps, SPAs
Example:
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

3️⃣ Session-Based Authentication
Server creates a session after login
Session ID is stored in a cookie
Server maintains session data
👉 Mostly used in traditional web applications

4️⃣ OAuth Authentication (Third-Party Login)
Login using Google, Facebook, GitHub, etc.
User is authenticated by third-party provider
Server receives access token
👉 Used for social logins

5️⃣ API Key Authentication
Client sends an API key with every request
Server validates the API key
👉 Used for internal services and public APIs
Example:
x-api-key: abc123

6️⃣ Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA / 2FA)
Uses more than one verification method
Example: Password + OTP
👉 Used in banking and secure systems
